            <div xml:id="d915">

                <pb facs="1100" n="990" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg990"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5034 Business Tax/3: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-03-06T17:00:00-05:00">March 6, 1931—5
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>85. Your 93, March 1, 3 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>You will be guided by Department’s 62, February 20, 5 p.m., in answering
                        inquiries from consular officers. However, Department perceives no objection
                        to consular officers’ pointing out to American firms who may apply to them
                        for advice practical aspects of situation as set forth in your 93, Section
                        5.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>In view of summary of regulations contained in your 71, February 16, 7
                        p.m., Section 1, Department considers that, in event of attempt by Chinese
                        authorities to enforce regulations against American firms, you would be
                        justified in making representations to Nanking Government.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Department desires full information by mail, including “general outline”
                        referred to in your 93, Section 3, and text of regulations.<anchor n="27"
                            xml:id="d915-f1"/></item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
